uber reveals that Y Combinator owns about 0.6 percent of OpenAI, worth over $5 billion at OpenAI's current $852 billion valuation.\",\n    \"author\": \"John Gruber (via Simon Willison)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-05\",\n    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"Y Combinator\", \"investments\", \"AI valuation\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AI Programming Platform 2.0 Launches with Multi-Agent Collaboration\",\n    \"description\": \"Major AI programming platforms are launching 2.0 versions with multi-agent collaboration systems, improving complex problem-solving accuracy by 30%. Cursor, developed by Anysphere and built on VS Code, leads with deep AI integration throughout the development workflow.\",\n    \"author\": \"Platform Updates\",\n    \"source\": \"Platform\",\n    \"url\": \"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2011954028528038812\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-04\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Cursor\", \"multi-agent systems\", \"AI platforms\", \"VS Code\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"IBM Releases Apache 2.0 Licensed Granite 4.1 LLMs\",\n    \"description\": \"IBM released Granite 4.1 family of LLMs in 3B, 8B and 30B sizes, all Apache 2.0 licensed. Simon Willison conducted experiments testing SVG generation across different quantized variants.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-04\",\n    \"topics\": [\"IBM\", \"LLM\", \"open source\", \"Granite\", \"generative AI\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Natural Language Programming Becomes Viable in 2026\",\n    \"description\": \"Programming barriers are being lowered as natural language becomes a viable way to create software, making development more accessible. This marks a fundamental shift from specification-driven development to AI agent-driven 