ge-break-inside: avoid;\n   253→            }\n   254→        }\n   255→    </style>\n   256→</head>\n   257→<body>\n   258→    <div class=\"container\">\n   259→        <header>\n   260→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   261→            <div class=\"subtitle\">Daily insights on AI programming tools and agent development • May 7, 2026</div>\n   262→        </header>\n   263→\n   264→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   265→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   266→                <h2>New Products</h2>\n   267→                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   268→                    No new products found in this research cycle.\n   269→                </div>\n   270→            </section>\n   271→\n   272→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   273→                <h2>Product Updates</h2>\n   274→\n   275→                <div class=\"item\">\n   276→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   277→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span>\n   278→                        <span class=\"version\">v2.1.132</span>\n   279→                    </div>\n   280→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   281→                        Multiple bug fixes and improvements including session ID environment variable, alternate screen opt-out, improved SIGINT handling, terminal fixes for various IDEs, and MCP server error handling improvements.\n   282→                    </div>\n   283→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   284→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   285→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   286→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.132\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Release Notes</a>\n   287→                    </div>\n   288→                </div>\n   289→\n   290→                <div class=\"item\">\n   291→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   292→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span>\n   293→                        <span class=\"version\">3.3</span>\n   294→                    </div>\n   295→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   296→                        Context usage breakdown feature allowing developers to see detailed stats about agent's context consumption across rules, skills, MCPs, and subagents to diagnose issues and optimize setup.\n   297→                    </div>\n   298→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   299→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   300→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   301→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog/05-06-26\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Changelog</a>\n   302→                    </div>\n   303→                </div>\n   304→\n   305→                <div class=\"item\">\n   306→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   307→                        <span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot CLI</span>\n   308→                    </div>\n   309→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   310→                        Enterprise-managed plugins in public preview, allowing organizations to control and manage CLI plugin access and configuration for their teams.\n   311→                    </div>\n   312→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   313→                        <span class=\"update-type\">announcement</span>\n   314→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   315→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-05-06-enterprise-managed-plugins-in-github-copilot-cli-are-now-in-public-preview\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Details</a>\n   316→                    </div>\n   317→                </div>\n   318→\n   319→                <div class=\"item\">\n   320→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   321→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf IDE</span>\n   322→                        <span class=\"version\">v2.2.17</span>\n   323→                    </div>\n   324→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   325→                        Devin Review and Quick Review now available to all users, Agent Command Center improvements with list display, better session sorting/filtering, and Windows update bug fixes.\n   326→                    </div>\n   327→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   328→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   329→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   330→                        <a href=\"https://codeium.com/changelog\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Changelog</a>\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                </div>\n   333→\n   334→                <div class=\"item\">\n   335→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   336→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span>\n   337→                    </div>\n   338→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   339→                        Support for Claude 4.5/4.6 models, expanded Gemini model support (2.5 Flash, Flash-Lite, Gemini 3 preview), DeepSeek Reasoner model, and new OpenAI GPT-5.1/5.2/5.3/5.4 models across providers.\n   340→                    </div>\n   341→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   342→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   343→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   344→                        <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ History</a>\n   345→                    </div>\n   346→                </div>\n   347→\n   348→                <div class=\"item\">\n   349→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   350→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Continue</span>\n   351→                        <span class=\"version\">v1.3.38</span>\n   352→                    </div>\n   353→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   354→                        Introduces .continue/configs support, workspace directory session history filtering, config.yaml existence checks, and multiple dependency updates.\n   355→                    </div>\n   356→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   357→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   358→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   359→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Releases</a>\n   360→                    </div>\n   361→                </div>\n   362→\n   363→                <div class=\"item\">\n   364→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   365→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span>\n   366→                    </div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   368→                        Enterprise admin updates including granular model access controls at provider/model level, updated spend management, and enhanced usage analytics with option to block new providers by default.\n   369→                    </div>\n   370→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   371→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   372→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-05-04</span>\n   373→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog/05-04-26\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Changelog</a>\n   374→                    </div>\n   375→                </div>\n   376→\n   377→                <div class=\"item\">\n   378→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   379→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Codex CLI</span>\n   380→                        <span class=\"version\">v0.128.0</span>\n   381→                    </div>\n   382→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   383→                        Persisted /goal workflows, configurable TUI keymaps, plan-mode nudges, expanded permission profiles with sandbox controls, improved plugin workflows, and MultiAgentV2 enhancements.\n   384→                    </div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   386→                        <span class=\"update-type\">release</span>\n   387→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-04-30</span>\n   388→                        <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Changelog</a>\n   389→                    </div>\n   390→                </div>\n   391→\n   392→                <div class=\"item\">\n   393→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   394→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Devin</span>\n   395→                    </div>\n   396→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   397→                        Sensitive toggle for secrets (masked/visible), merged multi-edits in progress tab showing combined diffs, session category/subcategory in v3 API, and wide markdown tables in chat.\n   398→                    </div>\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   400→                        <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   401→                        <span class=\"date\">2026-04-24</span>\n   402→                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" class=\"external-link\" target=\"_blank\">→ Release Notes</a>\n   403→                    </div>\n   404→                </div>\n   405→            </section>\n   406→\n   407→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   408→                <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   409→\n   410→                <div class=\"item\">\n   411→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   412→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">MongoDB.local London 2026: AI Production</a>\n   413→                    </div>\n   414→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   415→                        MongoDB.local London 2026 event focuses on helping teams move AI from prototype to production, reflecting the industry shift from experimental AI to production-ready AI systems.\n   416→                    </div>\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   418→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   419→                        <span class=\"source\">MongoDB</span>\n   420→                        <span class=\"date\">May 7</span>\n   421→                    </div>\n   422→                </div>\n   423→\n   424→                <div class=\"item\">\n   425→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   426→                        <a href=\"https://www.hubwiz.com/blog\" target=\"_blank\">AI Will Augment, Not Replace Programmers</a>\n   427→                    </div>\n   428→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   429→                        Industry consensus emphasizes AI will augment programmer capabilities. Developers advised to focus on learning to work effectively with AI agents while maintaining classic software engineering principles.\n   430→                    </div>\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   432→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   433→                        <span class=\"source\">TechMedia</span>\n   434→                        <span class=\"date\">May 6</span>\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                </div>\n   437→\n   438→                <div class=\"item\">\n   439→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   440→                        <a href=\"https://www.hubwiz.com/blog\" target=\"_blank\">AI Coding Tools Market Validation</a>\n   441→                    </div>\n   442→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   443→                        Overseas markets validate AI coding tools value, while domestic markets enter high growth period. Enterprise CTOs focus shifts from 'completion speed' to 'engineering capability ceiling'.\n   444→                    </div>\n   445→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   446→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   447→                        <span class=\"source\">TechMedia</span>\n   448→                        <span class=\"date\">May 5</span>\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                </div>\n   451→\n   452→                <div class=\"item\">\n   453→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   454→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Y Combinator's $5B OpenAI Stake</a>\n   455→                    </div>\n   456→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   457→                        John Gruber reveals Y Combinator owns about 0.6% of OpenAI, worth over $5 billion at OpenAI's current $852 billion valuation.\n   458→                    </div>\n   459→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   460→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   461→                        <span class=\"source\">John Gruber</span>\n   462→                        <span class=\"date\">May 5</span>\n   463→                    </div>\n   464→                </div>\n   465→\n   466→                <div class=\"item\">\n   467→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   468→                        <a href=\"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2011954028528038812\" target=\"_blank\">AI Programming Platform 2.0 Era</a>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   471→                        Major AI programming platforms launching 2.0 versions with multi-agent collaboration systems, improving complex problem-solving accuracy by 30%.\n   472→                    </div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   474→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   475→                        <span class=\"source\">Platform Updates</span>\n   476→                        <span class=\"date\">May 4</span>\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→                </div>\n   479→\n   480→                <div class=\"item\">\n   481→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   482→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">IBM Granite 4.1 Apache 2.0 LLMs</a>\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   485→                        IBM released Granite 4.1 family of LLMs in 3B, 8B and 30B sizes, all Apache 2.0 licensed. Experiments testing SVG generation across different quantized variants.\n   486→                    </div>\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   488→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   489→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   490→                        <span class=\"date\">May 4</span>\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                </div>\n   493→\n   494→                <div class=\"item\">\n   495→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   496→                        <a href=\"https://www.hubwiz.com/blog\" target=\"_blank\">Natural Language Programming Viability</a>\n   497→                    </div>\n   498→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   499→                        Programming barriers lowering as natural language becomes viable for creating software, marking fundamental shift from specification-driven to AI agent-driven development.\n   500→                    </div>\n   501→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   502→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   503→                        <span class=\"source\">Industry Analysts</span>\n   504→                        <span class=\"date\">May 3</span>\n   505→                    </div>\n   506→                </div>\n   507→\n   508→                <div class=\"item\">\n   509→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   510→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">AI-Assisted Redis & WASM Development</a>\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   513→                        Claude Code used to build experimental Python binding for TRE regex library and interactive playground for Redis's new array data type commands.\n   514→                    </div>\n   515→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   516→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   517→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   518→                        <span class=\"date\">May 3</span>\n   519→                    </div>\n   520→                </div>\n   521→\n   522→                <div class=\"item\">\n   523→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   524→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Sycophancy Research</a>\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   527→                        Anthropic research shows Claude expresses sycophancy in 9% of conversations overall, jumping to 38% in spirituality and 25% in relationships.\n   528→                    </div>\n   529→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   530→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   531→                        <span class=\"source\">Anthropic</span>\n   532→                        <span class=\"date\">May 3</span>\n   533→                    </div>\n   534→                </div>\n   535→\n   536→                <div class=\"item\">\n   537→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   538→                        <a href=\"https://www.hubwiz.com/blog\" target=\"_blank\">Google's 2026 AI Integration</a>\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   541→                        Google engineering lead announces 2026 will see full AI integration across entire programming workflow while maintaining classic software engineering discipline.\n   542→                    </div>\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   544→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   545→                        <span class=\"source\">Google Engineering</span>\n   546→                        <span class=\"date\">May 2</span>\n   547→                    </div>\n   548→                </div>\n   549→\n   550→                <div class=\"item\">\n   551→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   552→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Mobile AI Development with Claude Code</a>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   555→                        Built iNaturalist Sightings feature entirely on phone using Claude Code for web, showing how AI coding tools enable development from mobile devices.\n   556→                    </div>\n   557→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   558→                        <span class=\"tag tutorial\">tutorial</span>\n   559→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   560→                        <span class=\"date\">May 2</span>\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                </div>\n   563→\n   564→                <div class=\"item\">\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   566→                        <a href=\"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2011954028528038812\" target=\"_blank\">Intelligent Agent Engineering Era</a>\n   567→                    </div>\n   568→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   569→                        AI programming shifted into era where AI systems can autonomously complete entire software development lifecycle. Multi-agent collaboration compresses timelines by 70%.\n   570→                    </div>\n   571→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   572→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   573→                        <span class=\"source\">AI Industry Analysis</span>\n   574→                        <span class=\"date\">May 1</span>\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→                </div>\n   577→\n   578→                <div class=\"item\">\n   579→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   580→                        <a href=\"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2011954028528038812\" target=\"_blank\">2026 AI Coding Tools Complete Guide</a>\n   581→                    </div>\n   582→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   583→                        Comprehensive guide covering IDEs with integrated AI, programming assistants, application builders, extensions and agents, code review and security tools, and documentation tools.\n   584→                    </div>\n   585→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   586→                        <span class=\"tag tutorial\">tutorial</span>\n   587→                        <span class=\"source\">Zhihu Tech Column</span>\n   588→                        <span class=\"date\">May 1</span>\n   589→                    </div>\n   590→                </div>\n   591→\n   592→                <div class=\"item\">\n   593→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   594→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">95% of Code AI-Assisted Claims Developer</a>\n   595→                    </div>\n   596→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   597→                        Developer states 95% of code produced without typing manually, writing much code on phone, highlighting dramatic shift toward AI-assisted coding.\n   598→                    </div>\n   599→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   600→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   601→                        <span class=\"source\">Podcast Guest</span>\n   602→                        <span class=\"date\">May 1</span>\n   603→                    </div>\n   604→                </div>\n   605→\n   606→                <div class=\"item\">\n   607→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   608→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Codex CLI /goal Feature</a>\n   609→                    </div>\n   610→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   611→                        Codex CLI adds /goal feature implementing 'Ralph loop' - keeps looping until goal completed or token budget exhausted using automatically injected prompts.\n   612→                    </div>\n   613→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   614→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   615→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   616→                        <span class=\"date\">Apr 30</span>\n   617→                    </div>\n   618→                </div>\n   619→\n   620→                <div class=\"item\">\n   621→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   622→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">UK AI Security Institute Evaluates GPT-5.5</a>\n   623→                    </div>\n   624→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   625→                        UK's AI Security Institute evaluated GPT-5.5 for finding security vulnerabilities and found it comparable to Claude Mythos. GPT-5.5 is generally available unlike Mythos.\n   626→                    </div>\n   627→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   628→                        <span class=\"tag technical\">technical</span>\n   629→                        <span class=\"source\">UK AI Security Institute</span>\n   630→                        <span class=\"date\">Apr 30</span>\n   631→                    </div>\n   632→                </div>\n   633→\n   634→                <div class=\"item\">\n   635→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   636→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Zig's Strict Anti-LLM Policy</a>\n   637→                    </div>\n   638→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   639→                        Zig bans LLMs for issues, PRs, and comments. Project bets on contributors, not contributions. LLM assistance breaks contributor growth, leading Bun not to upstream 4x performance improvements.\n   640→                    </div>\n   641→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   642→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   643→                        <span class=\"source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   644→                        <span class=\"date\">Apr 30</span>\n   645→                    </div>\n   646→                </div>\n   647→\n   648→                <div class=\"item\">\n   649→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   650→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">RSS for Vibe-Coded Apps Proposed</a>\n   651→                    </div>\n   652→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   653→                        Matt Webb argues vibe-coding accelerates app development, making apps more personal and frequent. Suggests RSS feeds for tools/apps pages with 'Install' buttons.\n   654→                    </div>\n   655→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   656→                        <span class=\"tag opinion\">opinion</span>\n   657→                        <span class=\"source\">Matt Webb</span>\n   658→                        <span class=\"date\">Apr 30</span>\n   659→                    </div>\n   660→                </div>\n   661→            </section>\n   662→        </main>\n   663→\n   664→        <footer>\n   665→            <p>Report generated by <strong>Agent Code Daily</strong> — Powered by <a href=\"https://claude.com/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Agent SDK</a></p>\n   666→            <p style=\"margin-top: 8px; color: #999999;\">Generated: 2026-05-07 | Data sourced from public APIs, blogs, and community forums</p>\n   667→        </footer>\n   668→    </div>\n   669→</body>\n   670→</html>"
      }
    ]
